uration":3.08,"text":"AI"},{"start":291.96,"duration":3.08,"text":"2021."},{"start":293.24,"duration":4.56,"text":"So, yes."},{"start":295.04,"duration":4.96,"text":"A lot of books are done in the same way."},{"start":297.8,"duration":4.2,"text":"So, we need different way to learn new"},{"start":300.0,"duration":5.52,"text":"things, okay?"},{"start":302.0,"duration":5.6,"text":"So, now we'll try to answer questions in"},{"start":305.52,"duration":4.08,"text":"a visual way."},{"start":307.6,"duration":3.96,"text":"Let's start with the beginning. What is"},{"start":309.6,"duration":4.8,"text":"Kubernetes?"},{"start":311.56,"duration":6.16,"text":"Kubernetes is an open source container"},{"start":314.4,"duration":5.28,"text":"orchestrator. Well, no."},{"start":317.72,"duration":4.52,"text":"That"},{"start":319.68,"duration":7.32,"text":"That doesn't explain that. Imagine"},{"start":322.24,"duration":4.76,"text":"Kubernetes as an orchestra conductor."},{"start":327.12,"duration":4.12,"text":"Declaratively,"},{"start":329.04,"duration":4.44,"text":"we ask the orchestra what we want and"},{"start":331.24,"duration":5.8,"text":"Kubernetes will do everything possible"},{"start":333.48,"duration":6.24,"text":"to ensure that this request is always"},{"start":337.04,"duration":5.24,"text":"respected. It will"},{"start":339.72,"duration":5.08,"text":"manage the resources, the machines, and"},{"start":342.28,"duration":5.84,"text":"the communication between containers"},{"start":344.8,"duration":6.6,"text":"both externally and internally."},{"start":348.12,"duration":6.04,"text":"To do this, we will write YAML manifest."},{"start":351.4,"duration":5.16,"text":"These are partitions that Kubernetes"},{"start":354.16,"duration":5.28,"text":"must follow."},{"start":356.56,"duration":4.52,"text":"Kubernetes is based on several"},{"start":359.44,"duration":5.08,"text":"components."},{"start":361.08,"duration":4.48,"text":"The The control plane"},{"start":364.52,"duration":4.4,"text":"contains"},{"start":365.56,"duration":4.64,"text":"several internal components such as the"},{"start":368.92,"duration":3.8,"text":"ETCD,"},{"start":370.2,"duration":5.84,"text":"the scheduler, the controller manager,"},{"start":372.72,"duration":8.12,"text":"and the API server that"},{"start":376.04,"duration":7.48,"text":"expose the API of the Kubernetes"},{"start":380.84,"duration":4.32,"text":"clusters. Please note that when you use"},{"start":383.52,"duration":4.2,"text":"a managed Kubernetes cluster with a"},{"start":385.16,"duration":4.68,"text":"cloud provider, the control plane will"},{"start":387.72,"duration":3.32,"text":"be managed by the"},{"start":389.84,"duration":2.28,"text":"cloud"},{"start":391.04,"duration":2.36,"text":"provider."},{"start":392.12,"duration":4.8,"text":"You"},{"start":393.4,"duration":6.52,"text":"You don't have to uh"},{"start":396.92,"duration":3.92,"text":"You don't have to manage it to update"},{"start":399.92,"duration":4.48,"text":"it."},{"start":400.84,"duration":4.68,"text":"You just have to focus on the developing"},{"start":404.4,"duration":4.88,"text":"and the"},{"start":405.52,"duration":5.88,"text":"deploying of your apps in the cluster."},{"start":409.28,"duration":4.32,"text":"And in the"},{"start":411.4,"duration":3.36,"text":"data plane, you have kubelet and"},{"start":413.6,"duration":4.56,"text":"kube-proxy,"},{"start":414.76,"duration":6.32,"text":"which run on each node."},{"start":418.16,"duration":5.48,"text":"We can We can interact with the API"},{"start":421.08,"duration":3.88,"text":"server of the Kubernetes cluster with"},{"start":423.64,"duration":2.48,"text":"kubectl,"},{"start":424.96,"duration":3.2,"text":"a"},{"start":426.12,"duration":3.84,"text":"command line tool."},{"start":428.16,"duration":3.4,"text":"A CLI."},{"start":429.96,"duration":3.12,"text":"A little"},{"start":431.56,"duration":2.8,"text":"disclaimer."},{"start":433.08,"duration":3.96,"text":"I said"},{"start":434.36,"duration":4.84,"text":"kubectl, but"},{"start":437.04,"duration":3.52,"text":"we can pro-"},{"start":439.2,"duration":4.68,"text":"pronounce it"},{"start":440.56,"duration":4.92,"text":"kubectl, kube, kube control."},{"start":443.88,"duration":4.36,"text":"It doesn't"},{"start":445.48,"duration":4.8,"text":"matter. The most important thing is"},{"start":448.24,"duration":6.32,"text":"is to use it."},{"start":450.28,"duration":9.48,"text":"Okay. So, we will try to"},{"start":454.56,"duration":8.8,"text":"explain several concepts in a visual way"},{"start":459.76,"duration":4.88,"text":"step by step. Let's start by the node."},{"start":463.36,"duration":5.12,"text":"A node"},{"start":464.64,"duration":6.08,"text":"is a physical or virtual"},{"start":468.48,"duration":7.76,"text":"machine."},{"start":470.72,"duration":10.28,"text":"A node provides CPU or GPU, memory,"},{"start":476.24,"duration":6.88,"text":"storage, and network connectivity."},{"start":481.0,"duration":4.16,"text":"Each node"},{"start":483.12,"duration":5.56,"text":"contains the services needed to run"},{"start":485.16,"duration":4.52,"text":"pods, such as the container runtime or"},{"start":488.68,"duration":3.08,"text":"kubelet."},{"start":489.68,"duration":4.24,"text":"Okay?"},{"start":491.76,"duration":5.12,"text":"Now, let's"},{"start":493.92,"duration":6.16,"text":"speak about pods."},{"start":496.88,"duration":6.68,"text":"Our applications, our workload,"},{"start":500.08,"duration":6.92,"text":"will run in containers,"},{"start":503.56,"duration":5.2,"text":"which themselves run in pods. Kubernetes"},{"start":507.0,"duration":4.12,"text":"is language"},{"start":508.76,"duration":6.76,"text":"agnostic, which means that you can"},{"start":511.12,"duration":8.44,"text":"develop your microservice in a lot of"},{"start":515.52,"duration":5.52,"text":"language, like in Java, Python, Go,"},{"start":519.56,"duration":6.2,"text":"etc."},{"start":521.04,"duration":7.84,"text":"A pod is the smallest deployable unit in"},{"start":525.76,"duration":3.12,"text":"a Kubernetes cluster."},{"start":529.12,"duration":5.68,"text":"A pod can"},{"start":530.8,"duration":7.56,"text":"contain one or several co-containers,"},{"start":534.8,"duration":5.36,"text":"and each pod has a unique IP"},{"start":538.36,"duration":5.76,"text":"address."},{"start":540.16,"duration":7.88,"text":"Our applications run in pods,"},{"start":544.12,"duration":5.92,"text":"which themselves run in nodes."},{"start":548.04,"duration":4.56,"text":"Okay, so it's cool, but what is"},{"start":550.04,"duration":5.64,"text":"happening when you ask Kubernetes to"},{"start":552.6,"duration":3.96,"text":"create a new pod? Hey Kubernetes, create"},{"start":555.68,"duration":2.04,"text":"a"},{"start":556.56,"duration":4.48,"text":"create a"},{"start":557.72,"duration":4.36,"text":"create a pod, please."},{"start":561.04,"duration":5.76,"text":"First,"},{"start":562.08,"duration":7.8,"text":"the API server receives the request and"},{"start":566.8,"duration":6.08,"text":"do some checks. It verifies the identity"},{"start":569.88,"duration":6.16,"text":"of the user. It's the authentication"},{"start":572.88,"duration":7.0,"text":"step. Who are you?"},{"start":576.04,"duration":8.6,"text":"And it check also if the user have the"},{"start":579.88,"duration":4.76,"text":"sufficient right to do it. If the"},{"start":584.76,"duration":4.64,"text":"authorization"},{"start":586.48,"duration":7.52,"text":"step. Are you guys all right?"},{"start":589.4,"duration":8.08,"text":"Then it save the state in the ETCD"},{"start":594.0,"duration":4.96,"text":"distributed then database."},{"start":597.48,"duration":5.4,"text":"At the time"},{"start":598.96,"duration":7.08,"text":"the API server will call the scheduler."},{"start":602.88,"duration":6.88,"text":"That will search which node, which"},{"start":606.04,"duration":7.88,"text":"machine is more convenient to place it"},{"start":609.76,"duration":6.16,"text":"according to CPU, GPU, memory, networks,"},{"start":613.92,"duration":5.0,"text":"and so on."},{"start":615.92,"duration":5.32,"text":"Scheduler can do it, but"},{"start":618.92,"duration":5.96,"text":"in order to help him, it's useful to"},{"start":621.24,"duration":6.76,"text":"define request in containers"},{"start":624.88,"duration":6.92,"text":"of a pod. Thanks to that"},{"start":628.0,"duration":5.8,"text":"the pod will be placed in the correct"},{"start":631.8,"duration":4.92,"text":"node."},{"start":633.8,"duration":5.48,"text":"Once placed by the scheduler, the pod is"},{"start":636.72,"duration":6.28,"text":"in pending state."},{"start":639.28,"duration":7.24,"text":"Then kubelet will attempt to pull"},{"start":643.0,"duration":7.92,"text":"the image from registry."},{"start":646.52,"duration":7.24,"text":"Once the image is retrieved"},{"start":650.92,"duration":4.88,"text":"kubelet creates the containers and"},{"start":653.76,"duration":5.4,"text":"starts them."},{"start":655.8,"duration":7.12,"text":"Then the pod is in running status and"},{"start":659.16,"duration":6.64,"text":"your application is finally started and"},{"start":662.92,"duration":5.52,"text":"and running. Okay?"},{"start":665.8,"duration":5.36,"text":"I cannot speak about Kubernetes without"},{"start":668.44,"duration":6.2,"text":"giving some tips. So, if you want to"},{"start":671.16,"duration":6.16,"text":"display the specific information of"},{"start":674.64,"duration":5.72,"text":"about a pod, you can type kubectl get"},{"start":677.32,"duration":5.32,"text":"pod and with JSON path"},{"start":680.36,"duration":6.04,"text":"you can"},{"start":682.64,"duration":6.04,"text":"display all the image of all the"},{"start":686.4,"duration":4.32,"text":"containers of a pod."},{"start":688.68,"duration":5.52,"text":"And you can delete immediately"},{"start":690.72,"duration":5.48,"text":"immediately your pods with force and"},{"start":694.2,"duration":3.12,"text":"grace period command."},{"start":696.2,"duration":2.48,"text":">> Okay."},{"start":697.32,"duration":4.52,"text":">> So, next"},{"start":698.68,"duration":6.56,"text":"let's talk about deployments."},{"start":701.84,"duration":4.44,"text":"Deployments are responsible for the pod"},{"start":705.24,"duration":3.48,"text":"they"},{"start":706.28,"duration":3.84,"text":"manage."},{"start":708.72,"duration":4.92,"text":"Stop."},{"start":710.12,"duration":6.08,"text":"So, if a pod become um"},{"start":713.64,"duration":5.16,"text":"unhealthy"},{"start":716.2,"duration":6.72,"text":"it will create a new pod"},{"start":718.8,"duration":6.68,"text":"and delete the old one. Bye-bye."},{"start":722.92,"duration":4.68,"text":"A deployment creates a replication a"},{"start":725.48,"duration":5.24,"text":"replication set"},{"start":727.6,"duration":7.0,"text":"which will create one"},{"start":730.72,"duration":7.88,"text":"or several pods depending on the of the"},{"start":734.6,"duration":6.16,"text":"number of specified replicas."},{"start":738.6,"duration":5.2,"text":"By scaling a deployment, we can easily"},{"start":740.76,"duration":7.08,"text":"change its its number of replicas. So,"},{"start":743.8,"duration":6.72,"text":"with the command kubectl scale"},{"start":747.84,"duration":4.16,"text":"we can scale the number of replicas to"},{"start":750.52,"duration":4.0,"text":"five."},{"start":752.0,"duration":3.88,"text":"So, the deployment"},{"start":754.52,"duration":2.76,"text":"will create"},{"start":755.88,"duration":3.04,"text":"one pod"},{"start":757.28,"duration":2.68,"text":"and one"},{"start":758.92,"duration":3.6,"text":"new pod."},{"start":759.96,"duration":5.56,"text":"So, at the end of the execution of the"},{"start":762.52,"duration":5.96,"text":"command, the new number of replicas will"},{"start":765.52,"duration":6.8,"text":"be equal to five. So, Kubernetes will"},{"start":768.48,"duration":8.28,"text":"ensure that at every moment we will have"},{"start":772.32,"duration":7.64,"text":"five pods for this deployment. And"},{"start":776.76,"duration":4.92,"text":"of course, you can scale down at every"},{"start":779.96,"duration":3.08,"text":"moment."},{"start":781.68,"duration":5.6,"text":"Okay?"},{"start":783.04,"duration":6.84,"text":"So, now let's talk about services."},{"start":787.28,"duration":6.04,"text":"Our application running pods"},{"start":789.88,"duration":6.56,"text":"and this pod are ephemeral."},{"start":793.32,"duration":4.4,"text":"Services allow allow us to access our"},{"start":796.44,"duration":5.24,"text":"application"},{"start":797.72,"duration":7.44,"text":"via unique IP address."},{"start":801.68,"duration":6.56,"text":"So, we will be able to assign a unique"},{"start":805.16,"duration":6.68,"text":"DNS name to a group of pod."},{"start":808.24,"duration":5.48,"text":"This will allow us to access our my zone"},{"start":811.84,"duration":5.12,"text":"application. So,"},{"start":813.72,"duration":6.04,"text":"if I do a curl in my zone application"},{"start":816.96,"duration":4.36,"text":"dot my name space dot as you see that"},{"start":819.76,"duration":2.6,"text":"the console that the local"},{"start":821.32,"duration":6.88,"text":"the"},{"start":822.36,"duration":7.32,"text":"traffic will be route to the service and"},{"start":828.2,"duration":3.28,"text":"and the"},{"start":829.68,"duration":5.84,"text":"from traffic"},{"start":831.48,"duration":7.16,"text":"will go to one pod."},{"start":835.52,"duration":5.96,"text":"The group of pod targeted by a service"},{"start":838.64,"duration":5.08,"text":"is usually determined by a sector. This"},{"start":841.48,"duration":2.24,"text":"is"},{"start":844.48,"duration":5.08,"text":"Several type of services"},{"start":847.44,"duration":5.88,"text":"exist."},{"start":849.56,"duration":6.32,"text":"Cluster IP is the default service type."},{"start":853.32,"duration":5.44,"text":"It allows you to expose a service"},{"start":855.88,"duration":6.12,"text":"through an IP address internal to the"},{"start":858.76,"duration":6.64,"text":"cluster. So, please note that that this"},{"start":862.0,"duration":6.24,"text":"type of service will only be accessible"},{"start":865.4,"duration":5.8,"text":"within the cluster."},{"start":868.24,"duration":8.72,"text":"The node port will be accessible outside"},{"start":871.2,"duration":9.4,"text":"the cluster but with the IP of the node."},{"start":876.96,"duration":6.88,"text":"The load balancer service I find a fixed"},{"start":880.6,"duration":6.24,"text":"IP address and create an external load"},{"start":883.84,"duration":6.76,"text":"balancer. So, this solution only works"},{"start":886.84,"duration":5.68,"text":"with external cloud provider."},{"start":890.6,"duration":4.64,"text":"So, in this"},{"start":892.52,"duration":4.32,"text":"example, we have our application running"},{"start":895.24,"duration":4.48,"text":"in a pod"},{"start":896.84,"duration":5.36,"text":"that is"},{"start":899.72,"duration":5.0,"text":"exposed through a service."},{"start":902.2,"duration":5.88,"text":"An external load balancer have been"},{"start":904.72,"duration":7.96,"text":"created and IP address have been created"},{"start":908.08,"duration":6.08,"text":"too. So, if I do a curl there"},{"start":912.68,"duration":4.44,"text":"I will have"},{"start":914.16,"duration":2.96,"text":"my application."},{"start":917.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"And the external name of service allows"},{"start":919.64,"duration":6.92,"text":"allows you to provide an internal alias"},{"start":923.16,"duration":5.28,"text":"for the clusters that would like to an"},{"start":926.56,"duration":4.36,"text":"external DNS"},{"start":928.44,"duration":2.48,"text":"address."},{"start":931.0,"duration":4.36,"text":"Okay."},{"start":932.08,"duration":4.68,"text":"Now, we we will talk about namespace."},{"start":935.36,"duration":4.6,"text":"What is it?"},{"start":936.76,"duration":4.72,"text":"A namespace is a form of isolation."},{"start":939.96,"duration":4.92,"text":"This allow you to isolate your"},{"start":941.48,"duration":6.68,"text":"application by project, by team, or by"},{"start":944.88,"duration":5.92,"text":"family of component."},{"start":948.16,"duration":5.68,"text":"Resource name but must be unique within"},{"start":950.8,"duration":6.52,"text":"a single namespace, but not across"},{"start":953.84,"duration":5.4,"text":"several namespace. So, you can't have"},{"start":957.32,"duration":4.96,"text":"two resources"},{"start":959.24,"duration":5.68,"text":"with the same name in a name- namespace."},{"start":962.28,"duration":6.56,"text":"That's possible. So,"},{"start":964.92,"duration":7.28,"text":"So, so So, you can have a one"},{"start":968.84,"duration":5.84,"text":"one service called my my service my"},{"start":972.2,"duration":5.32,"text":"service in namespace one and in"},{"start":974.68,"duration":5.68,"text":"namespace two, but you can't have the"},{"start":977.52,"duration":4.88,"text":"same name in the same name- name-"},{"start":980.36,"duration":4.64,"text":"namespace."},{"start":982.4,"duration":5.92,"text":"And be careful if you delete a"},{"start":985.0,"duration":6.76,"text":"namespace, all resources all resources"},{"start":988.32,"duration":6.52,"text":"inside will be deleted as well. It's a"},{"start":991.76,"duration":4.08,"text":"normal behavior, but it's useful to know"},{"start":994.84,"duration":4.2,"text":"it."},{"start":995.84,"duration":5.76,"text":"If you delete it, all the objects inside"},{"start":999.04,"duration":4.4,"text":"will be will be deleted"},{"start":1001.6,"duration":6.0,"text":"as well."},{"start":1003.44,"duration":8.0,"text":"And not all resources in in Kubernetes"},{"start":1007.6,"duration":8.24,"text":"are in a name- namespace. There are some"},{"start":1011.44,"duration":6.4,"text":"objects like a node that is"},{"start":1015.84,"duration":2.88,"text":"cluster-wide."},{"start":1017.84,"duration":3.8,"text":"Okay."},{"start":1018.72,"duration":6.48,"text":"After the namespace, let's explain what"},{"start":1021.64,"duration":7.48,"text":"is a quota, a resource quota."},{"start":1025.2,"duration":6.12,"text":"The resource quota limits the use and"},{"start":1029.12,"duration":5.8,"text":"the number of resources"},{"start":1031.32,"duration":5.76,"text":"that can be created and managed in a"},{"start":1034.92,"duration":5.16,"text":"name- namespace."},{"start":1037.08,"duration":6.52,"text":"When several work on several the"},{"start":1040.08,"duration":5.72,"text":"namespaces, a quota can be created for"},{"start":1043.6,"duration":5.4,"text":"each the namespace."},{"start":1045.8,"duration":5.96,"text":"With this example, it means that on the"},{"start":1049.0,"duration":5.48,"text":"my namespace one, we won't be able to"},{"start":1051.76,"duration":5.24,"text":"deploy more than four pods."},{"start":1054.48,"duration":6.2,"text":"And on my namespace two, we define the"},{"start":1057.0,"duration":5.4,"text":"total CPU and memory consumed by all the"},{"start":1060.68,"duration":5.24,"text":"pod in the namespace."},{"start":1062.4,"duration":8.12,"text":"And we can also control the maximum"},{"start":1065.92,"duration":7.4,"text":"number of secrets or volumes and so on."},{"start":1070.52,"duration":5.68,"text":"When requesting the creation of a new"},{"start":1073.32,"duration":5.12,"text":"object, the admission controller"},{"start":1076.2,"duration":4.28,"text":"check whether the quota will be"},{"start":1078.44,"duration":4.52,"text":"exceeded. If so,"},{"start":1080.48,"duration":5.4,"text":"an error message is displayed and the"},{"start":1082.96,"duration":4.76,"text":"creation will be"},{"start":1085.88,"duration":4.72,"text":"refused."},{"start":1087.72,"duration":6.12,"text":"Warning, if a quota is enabled with CPU"},{"start":1090.6,"duration":6.84,"text":"and memory, you must specify request and"},{"start":1093.84,"duration":7.28,"text":"limits for your pods."},{"start":1097.44,"duration":6.92,"text":"Now, let's talk about jobs."},{"start":1101.12,"duration":5.84,"text":"A job is a process that takes a certain"},{"start":1104.36,"duration":5.08,"text":"amount of time to execute."},{"start":1106.96,"duration":5.68,"text":"For example, a job can be created for"},{"start":1109.44,"duration":6.4,"text":"several use cases, a batch process,"},{"start":1112.64,"duration":5.4,"text":"a backup, a database migration, or a"},{"start":1115.84,"duration":7.56,"text":"cleanup."},{"start":1118.04,"duration":8.48,"text":"A job run one on one or several pods"},{"start":1123.4,"duration":5.52,"text":"and ensure that a specific number of"},{"start":1126.52,"duration":5.48,"text":"pods complete successfully. So,"},{"start":1128.92,"duration":4.32,"text":"currently, a pod created by a job have a"},{"start":1132.0,"duration":5.24,"text":"mission"},{"start":1133.24,"duration":7.08,"text":"and it's needed to complete it."},{"start":1137.24,"duration":6.12,"text":"A job can be executed once, it can be"},{"start":1140.32,"duration":6.52,"text":"sequential, or it can launch several"},{"start":1143.36,"duration":3.48,"text":"pods in parallel."},{"start":1146.92,"duration":6.32,"text":"If the pod fails,"},{"start":1150.08,"duration":7.28,"text":"another pod will run"},{"start":1153.24,"duration":6.76,"text":"until the number of pod successfully"},{"start":1157.36,"duration":2.64,"text":"complete."},{"start":1160.28,"duration":8.16,"text":"By default, completion is is set it to"},{"start":1164.52,"duration":7.36,"text":"one. So, if we set completion to three,"},{"start":1168.44,"duration":7.68,"text":"the job controller will spawn pods until"},{"start":1171.88,"duration":4.24,"text":"the number of completion is reached."},{"start":1176.48,"duration":5.28,"text":"And jobs can be"},{"start":1178.6,"duration":6.24,"text":"indexed. It means that you can configure"},{"start":1181.76,"duration":6.68,"text":"a job that will run several pods"},{"start":1184.84,"duration":4.84,"text":"that will process a different chunk of"},{"start":1188.44,"duration":4.28,"text":"data."},{"start":1189.68,"duration":5.76,"text":"And as pod as launched by job, for"},{"start":1192.72,"duration":5.96,"text":"example, if the if the pod responsible"},{"start":1195.44,"duration":5.72,"text":"to process a certain chunk of data"},{"start":1198.68,"duration":4.84,"text":"is what?"},{"start":1201.16,"duration":5.88,"text":"Failed."},{"start":1203.52,"duration":7.48,"text":"Another pod will be created until its"},{"start":1207.04,"duration":3.96,"text":"mission is complete."},{"start":1211.04,"duration":5.2,"text":"Now, let's talk about cron jobs."},{"start":1216.32,"duration":5.36,"text":"Cron jobs allows you to launch scheduled"},{"start":1220.0,"duration":4.28,"text":"task."},{"start":1221.68,"duration":2.6,"text":"Basically,"},{"start":1224.32,"duration":9.16,"text":"so a cron job launch a job"},{"start":1228.56,"duration":8.56,"text":"which can launch one or several pods."},{"start":1233.48,"duration":4.92,"text":"It's useful, for example, for database"},{"start":1237.12,"duration":5.2,"text":"backup,"},{"start":1238.4,"duration":7.8,"text":"clean up task, and any type of periodic"},{"start":1242.32,"duration":8.72,"text":"task like a mail sender."},{"start":1246.2,"duration":6.04,"text":"It is based on a cron format."},{"start":1251.04,"duration":6.64,"text":"Okay."},{"start":1252.24,"duration":9.44,"text":"So, our application run in pods"},{"start":1257.68,"duration":7.64,"text":"controlled by a deployment that are"},{"start":1261.68,"duration":5.64,"text":"exposed through services. And"},{"start":1265.32,"duration":3.88,"text":"I can launch launch some batch"},{"start":1267.32,"duration":4.36,"text":"processes, but what about the"},{"start":1269.2,"duration":4.64,"text":"configuration and what about the"},{"start":1271.68,"duration":6.04,"text":"environment variables?"},{"start":1273.84,"duration":7.72,"text":"Let's talk about config map."},{"start":1277.72,"duration":7.12,"text":"Config map answered to one of the 12"},{"start":1281.56,"duration":6.4,"text":"factor app for parents of microservice."},{"start":1284.84,"duration":4.16,"text":"Do not hardcode configuration in your"},{"start":1287.96,"duration":4.72,"text":"apps."},{"start":1289.0,"duration":8.84,"text":"Instead, the best practice is to store"},{"start":1292.68,"duration":6.52,"text":"non-sensitive data in a config map."},{"start":1297.84,"duration":3.56,"text":"This allows"},{"start":1299.2,"duration":6.68,"text":"This allows you to separate"},{"start":1301.4,"duration":7.0,"text":"configuration from pods."},{"start":1305.88,"duration":5.48,"text":"And thanks to that, you can"},{"start":1308.4,"duration":5.4,"text":"deploy a same application in different"},{"start":1311.36,"duration":5.2,"text":"environment. So,"},{"start":1313.8,"duration":5.64,"text":"you can deploy an app in production,"},{"start":1316.56,"duration":4.56,"text":"staging, QA, and so on."},{"start":1319.44,"duration":4.0,"text":"So, for example,"},{"start":1321.12,"duration":5.28,"text":"you can define a particular"},{"start":1323.44,"duration":5.2,"text":"configuration parameter for staging"},{"start":1326.4,"duration":5.72,"text":"environment and other one for the"},{"start":1328.64,"duration":6.16,"text":"production. So, for example, the URL and"},{"start":1332.12,"duration":4.52,"text":"the port of option"},{"start":1334.8,"duration":4.24,"text":"to the base will be"},{"start":1336.64,"duration":5.12,"text":"different."},{"start":1339.04,"duration":4.68,"text":"A config map can contains a config"},{"start":1341.76,"duration":3.8,"text":"configuration files like a"},{"start":1343.72,"duration":2.64,"text":"config.properties"},{"start":1345.56,"duration":3.0,"text":"or"},{"start":1346.36,"duration":4.24,"text":"or an"},{"start":1348.56,"duration":5.56,"text":"engine accounts"},{"start":1350.6,"duration":7.2,"text":"or one or several key-value pairs,"},{"start":1354.12,"duration":11.0,"text":"one or several environment variables,"},{"start":1357.8,"duration":7.32,"text":"or a binary that is encoded in base64."},{"start":1365.16,"duration":5.44,"text":"We can create a config map from three"},{"start":1368.96,"duration":4.64,"text":"different sources."},{"start":1370.6,"duration":6.08,"text":"From a key-value. So, for for for"},{"start":1373.6,"duration":6.16,"text":"example, we have a config map named my"},{"start":1376.68,"duration":7.0,"text":"CM and we can"},{"start":1379.76,"duration":5.92,"text":"define some parameters like the like a"},{"start":1383.68,"duration":5.52,"text":"threshold and"},{"start":1385.68,"duration":5.4,"text":"maximum quantity of connection for for a"},{"start":1389.2,"duration":3.92,"text":"DB."},{"start":1391.08,"duration":3.04,"text":"We can also create a config map from a"},{"start":1393.12,"duration":3.24,"text":"file."},{"start":1394.12,"duration":3.76,"text":"So, there"},{"start":1396.36,"duration":4.6,"text":"So, there like"},{"start":1397.88,"duration":5.84,"text":"there is an example with an"},{"start":1400.96,"duration":5.48,"text":"engine x config file."},{"start":1403.72,"duration":4.48,"text":"And we can also create one for an"},{"start":1406.44,"duration":3.16,"text":"environment variable."},{"start":1408.2,"duration":3.08,"text":"So,"},{"start":1409.6,"duration":4.88,"text":"we can list"},{"start":1411.28,"duration":5.84,"text":"one or several environment variables."},{"start":1414.48,"duration":7.64,"text":"For example, with the"},{"start":1417.12,"duration":5.0,"text":"host of the DB and at the port."},{"start":1422.48,"duration":6.32,"text":"To prevent accidental"},{"start":1425.28,"duration":5.12,"text":"or unwanted change, a config map can be"},{"start":1428.8,"duration":3.44,"text":"can be an"},{"start":1430.4,"duration":4.28,"text":"immutable."},{"start":1432.24,"duration":5.6,"text":"It can be convenient because an"},{"start":1434.68,"duration":4.32,"text":"application should only need to read"},{"start":1437.84,"duration":4.2,"text":"a"},{"start":1439.0,"duration":7.04,"text":"configuration. But, it means that if you"},{"start":1442.04,"duration":4.0,"text":"want to update the"},{"start":1446.76,"duration":6.92,"text":"config map, you have to um"},{"start":1449.76,"duration":5.04,"text":"you have to restart the the pod."},{"start":1453.68,"duration":6.32,"text":"So,"},{"start":1454.8,"duration":8.12,"text":"it's So, it's very use- useful, but not"},{"start":1460.0,"duration":7.28,"text":"really used now."},{"start":1462.92,"duration":8.88,"text":"Be careful. A pod that is in the"},{"start":1467.28,"duration":7.36,"text":"namespace A cannot read a config map"},{"start":1471.8,"duration":4.08,"text":"that is in an"},{"start":1474.64,"duration":3.16,"text":"another"},{"start":1475.88,"duration":3.08,"text":"name- namespace."},{"start":1477.8,"duration":5.12,"text":"It is"},{"start":1478.96,"duration":6.68,"text":"ne- necessary that the resources related"},{"start":1482.92,"duration":3.84,"text":"to a pod are in the same name-"},{"start":1485.64,"duration":4.4,"text":"namespace."},{"start":1486.76,"duration":3.28,"text":"It's really important."},{"start":1490.32,"duration":6.88,"text":"And the last concept we'll see today"},{"start":1493.64,"duration":7.16,"text":"is the secret. Secrets allow you to save"},{"start":1497.2,"duration":7.6,"text":"sensitive data such as password, token,"},{"start":1500.8,"duration":6.76,"text":"credential, access key, or certificate."},{"start":1504.8,"duration":4.0,"text":"The secrets are encoded in base in base"},{"start":1507.56,"duration":3.76,"text":"64"},{"start":1508.8,"duration":4.64,"text":"and automatically decoded when read and"},{"start":1511.32,"duration":3.32,"text":"attached to a pod."},{"start":1513.44,"duration":4.72,"text":"Warning,"},{"start":1514.64,"duration":6.56,"text":"unencoded is not something like"},{"start":1518.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"encrypted. So, the secrets are not"},{"start":1521.2,"duration":4.6,"text":"really secrets in a Kubernetes"},{"start":1524.16,"duration":5.64,"text":"cluster."},{"start":1525.8,"duration":7.2,"text":"So, if someone retrieves a secret, he or"},{"start":1529.8,"duration":6.2,"text":"she just have to decode it in in base"},{"start":1533.0,"duration":5.48,"text":"64. Well,"},{"start":1536.0,"duration":4.64,"text":"it's not really really really easy"},{"start":1538.48,"duration":5.68,"text":"because"},{"start":1540.64,"duration":5.6,"text":"you have to get a secret with the name"},{"start":1544.16,"duration":3.28,"text":"of the namespace, with name of the"},{"start":1546.24,"duration":4.4,"text":"secret."},{"start":1547.44,"duration":6.08,"text":"You have to output it in JSON,"},{"start":1550.64,"duration":5.84,"text":"and you have to know what is the sub"},{"start":1553.52,"duration":5.8,"text":"field in secret, and then you have to"},{"start":1556.48,"duration":4.04,"text":"decode it. It's not really easy."},{"start":1559.32,"duration":4.6,"text":"But,"},{"start":1560.52,"duration":7.48,"text":"I have a a tips. You can use"},{"start":1563.92,"duration":4.08,"text":"the kubectl view secret"},{"start":1568.24,"duration":4.16,"text":"plugin. It"},{"start":1569.92,"duration":4.72,"text":"it it can"},{"start":1572.4,"duration":3.44,"text":"help you to"},{"start":1574.64,"duration":3.56,"text":"to type"},{"start":1575.84,"duration":4.44,"text":"this kind of command, and it's really"},{"start":1578.2,"duration":4.0,"text":"really really really good."},{"start":1580.28,"duration":5.04,"text":"Like a config map, you can create a"},{"start":1582.2,"duration":6.24,"text":"secret for three different sources, from"},{"start":1585.32,"duration":4.92,"text":"one or several key and value,"},{"start":1588.44,"duration":4.88,"text":"from a file,"},{"start":1590.24,"duration":5.84,"text":"or from an environment variable file."},{"start":1593.32,"duration":4.12,"text":"There are three types of secrets,"},{"start":1596.08,"duration":5.28,"text":"generic,"},{"start":1597.44,"duration":6.48,"text":"Docker registry, and TLS. Generic is a"},{"start":1601.36,"duration":3.92,"text":"secret created from a file."},{"start":1603.92,"duration":4.56,"text":"There."},{"start":1605.28,"duration":6.88,"text":"Docker registry is a Docker config"},{"start":1608.48,"duration":5.84,"text":"secret that allows a pod to authenticate"},{"start":1612.16,"duration":6.24,"text":"to a Docker registry."},{"start":1614.32,"duration":5.84,"text":"And TLS is for TLS or mutual TLS"},{"start":1618.4,"duration":6.2,"text":"certificate."},{"start":1620.16,"duration":7.68,"text":"Like a config map, a pod that is in that"},{"start":1624.6,"duration":4.96,"text":"is in the namespace A country the secret"},{"start":1627.84,"duration":4.52,"text":"that is in um"},{"start":1629.56,"duration":6.96,"text":"the Facebook. Okay?"},{"start":1632.36,"duration":5.04,"text":"A lot of concepts exist, but my time is"},{"start":1636.52,"duration":2.08,"text":"uh"},{"start":1637.4,"duration":3.28,"text":"is uh"},{"start":1638.6,"duration":4.04,"text":"almost uh over now."},{"start":1640.68,"duration":5.8,"text":"And the good thing is that everything we"},{"start":1642.64,"duration":7.64,"text":"saw, we can do it for example at oh"},{"start":1646.48,"duration":6.48,"text":"at OVH Cloud. We have a solution of"},{"start":1650.28,"duration":7.0,"text":"managed Kubernetes"},{"start":1652.96,"duration":5.04,"text":"clusters, and we have also a solution to"},{"start":1657.28,"duration":3.28,"text":"uh"},{"start":1658.0,"duration":4.96,"text":"to store your"},{"start":1660.56,"duration":3.2,"text":"to store your Docker in"},{"start":1662.96,"duration":2.12,"text":"in"},{"start":1663.76,"duration":5.48,"text":"images."},{"start":1665.08,"duration":6.48,"text":"And also, you can manage all of your"},{"start":1669.24,"duration":4.36,"text":"Kubernetes"},{"start":1671.56,"duration":5.08,"text":"clusters"},{"start":1673.6,"duration":4.8,"text":"even if they are Google, Amazon, or"},{"start":1676.64,"duration":4.88,"text":"Microsoft."},{"start":1678.4,"duration":5.08,"text":"And you can deploy your Kubernetes"},{"start":1681.52,"duration":4.56,"text":"cluster with Terraform,"},{"start":1683.48,"duration":6.0,"text":"with Pulumi,"},{"start":1686.08,"duration":5.76,"text":"and with a CLI. Okay."},{"start":1689.48,"duration":4.84,"text":"To con- conclude,"},{"start":1691.84,"duration":5.24,"text":"by listening to my creativity and my"},{"start":1694.32,"duration":5.84,"text":"imagination during a not easy period of"},{"start":1697.08,"duration":5.4,"text":"my life, I created a new way of"},{"start":1700.16,"duration":5.32,"text":"explaining complicated technical"},{"start":1702.48,"duration":6.44,"text":"concepts, and I showed that it it was"},{"start":1705.48,"duration":5.88,"text":"possible. And I realized that my"},{"start":1708.92,"duration":5.72,"text":"way of explaining could help other"},{"start":1711.36,"duration":6.44,"text":"people of different job and"},{"start":1714.64,"duration":4.8,"text":"ages and con- and"},{"start":1717.8,"duration":3.8,"text":"continents."},{"start":1719.44,"duration":3.56,"text":"And my"},{"start":1721.6,"duration":3.96,"text":"purpose"},{"start":1723.0,"duration":5.4,"text":"of this talk is to encourage you to"},{"start":1725.56,"duration":4.76,"text":"listen to your own imagination and your"},{"start":1728.4,"duration":4.88,"text":"own creativity"},{"start":1730.32,"duration":6.16,"text":"and share it them other ways."},{"start":1733.28,"duration":6.12,"text":"So, it's really important to find your"},{"start":1736.48,"duration":5.18,"text":"personal way to share."},{"start":1739.4,"duration":4.28,"text":"Thank you. Thank you."},{"start":1741.66,"duration":2.02,"text":">> [applause]"}]}